INSERT INTO `rag_chat_messages` VALUES (1,1,'USER','Will Azure AD SSO configuration be completed by the 25 April deadline?',NULL,'2026-07-27 07:02:17'),(2,1,'ASSISTANT','Based on the project documentation, it is unlikely that the Azure AD SSO configuration will be completed by the 25 April 2026 deadline.\n\n1. **Current Status**: According to the Weekly Status Report dated 18 April 2026, the configuration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold. This information is found in Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf, page 1.\n\n2. **Reason for Delay**: The progress is stalled because the necessary VPN connectivity and API credentials, which are the responsibility of the client, remain pending. This is confirmed by the discussion summary and action items located in Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf, page 1.\n\n3. **Scope Baseline**: The Structured Scope Items (Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones.pdf) confirm that the vendor is responsible for configuring Azure AD SSO by the 25 April 2026 deadline, but this remains dependent on the client providing the required infrastructure access mentioned above.','[{\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Minutes of Meeting (MoM) / Weekly Status Report\\nProject: Internal Support Portal Implementation\\nDate: 18 April 2026\\nLocation: Microsoft Teams\\nAttendees: Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Lead, QA Lead, Client Representative\\nAgenda\\n• Review implementation progress.\\n• Discuss open blockers.\\n• Review client enhancement requests.\\n• Plan activities for next sprint.\\nDiscussion Summary\\nCRM Integration development has been completed and handed over to the QA team for system\\ntesting.\\nConfiguration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold because VPN connectivity and API\\ncredentials from the client are still pending.\\nDevelopment of the Analytics Dashboard is progressing well and is estimated to be around 60%\\ncomplete.\\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT) has been rescheduled because dependent integration activities\\nhave not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\", \"document_id\": 19, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"• Project Manager to assess SAP Integration request.\\n• Technical team to prepare the UAT environment.\\nNext Meeting: 25 April 2026\", \"document_id\": 19, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"have not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\\nKnowledge Transfer sessions will be finalized after confirmation of the deployment timeline.\\nDuring the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform. The\\nproject manager agreed to evaluate the request and discuss effort estimation in the next steering\\ncommittee meeting.\\nThe client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access\\nthe portal remotely. The request will be reviewed separately.\\nA Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\\nThe client team agreed to provide API credentials, VPN access, and production environment details\\nbefore the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\", \"document_id\": 19, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"before the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\\n• Client to enable VPN connectivity for integration testing.\\n• QA team to begin CRM Integration testing.\", \"document_id\": 19, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}]','2026-07-27 07:02:17'),(3,2,'USER','Are there specific API limitations for the AI Knowledge Search feature?',NULL,'2026-07-27 13:20:40'),(4,2,'ASSISTANT','I cannot find information regarding specific API limitations for the AI Knowledge Search feature in the provided project documents or the structured scope items.\n\nWhile the project documentation confirms that the implementation of AI Knowledge Search is an active, in-scope item as defined in the Sample Engagement Letter with Milestones (Page 1), there is no mention of technical or API-specific constraints associated with this feature.','[{\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Sample Engagement Letter (ACSE Test Document)\\nProject Scope\\nThe Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal.\\nThe Vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search.\\nThe Vendor shall implement CRM Integration by 15 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall configure Azure AD SSO by 25 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall develop an Analytics Dashboard.\\nThe Vendor shall conduct UAT by 15 May 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall perform Production Deployment (Go Live) on 30 June 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall provide Knowledge Transfer by 05 July 2026.\\nOut of Scope\\nNative Android and iOS applications are excluded.\\nVoice Bot implementation is out of scope.\\nThird-party software licenses remain customer responsibility.\\n24x7 Production Support is not included in this engagement.\\nMilestones\\nCRM Integration - 15 April 2026\\nAzure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Azure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\\nCustomer shall provide required infrastructure before implementation.\\nChange Control\\nAny work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"have not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\\nKnowledge Transfer sessions will be finalized after confirmation of the deployment timeline.\\nDuring the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform. The\\nproject manager agreed to evaluate the request and discuss effort estimation in the next steering\\ncommittee meeting.\\nThe client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access\\nthe portal remotely. The request will be reviewed separately.\\nA Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\\nThe client team agreed to provide API credentials, VPN access, and production environment details\\nbefore the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"before the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\\n• Client to enable VPN connectivity for integration testing.\\n• QA team to begin CRM Integration testing.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Minutes of Meeting (MoM) / Weekly Status Report\\nProject: Internal Support Portal Implementation\\nDate: 18 April 2026\\nLocation: Microsoft Teams\\nAttendees: Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Lead, QA Lead, Client Representative\\nAgenda\\n• Review implementation progress.\\n• Discuss open blockers.\\n• Review client enhancement requests.\\n• Plan activities for next sprint.\\nDiscussion Summary\\nCRM Integration development has been completed and handed over to the QA team for system\\ntesting.\\nConfiguration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold because VPN connectivity and API\\ncredentials from the client are still pending.\\nDevelopment of the Analytics Dashboard is progressing well and is estimated to be around 60%\\ncomplete.\\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT) has been rescheduled because dependent integration activities\\nhave not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"• Project Manager to assess SAP Integration request.\\n• Technical team to prepare the UAT environment.\\nNext Meeting: 25 April 2026\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}]','2026-07-27 13:20:41'),(5,2,'USER','Are there specific API limitations for the AI Knowledge Search feature?',NULL,'2026-07-27 13:20:50'),(6,2,'ASSISTANT','I cannot find the answer in the project documents.\n\nThe provided project scope and documentation mention that the vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search as part of the project baseline, but there is no information detailing specific API limitations associated with this feature.','[{\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Sample Engagement Letter (ACSE Test Document)\\nProject Scope\\nThe Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal.\\nThe Vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search.\\nThe Vendor shall implement CRM Integration by 15 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall configure Azure AD SSO by 25 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall develop an Analytics Dashboard.\\nThe Vendor shall conduct UAT by 15 May 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall perform Production Deployment (Go Live) on 30 June 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall provide Knowledge Transfer by 05 July 2026.\\nOut of Scope\\nNative Android and iOS applications are excluded.\\nVoice Bot implementation is out of scope.\\nThird-party software licenses remain customer responsibility.\\n24x7 Production Support is not included in this engagement.\\nMilestones\\nCRM Integration - 15 April 2026\\nAzure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Azure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\\nCustomer shall provide required infrastructure before implementation.\\nChange Control\\nAny work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"have not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\\nKnowledge Transfer sessions will be finalized after confirmation of the deployment timeline.\\nDuring the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform. The\\nproject manager agreed to evaluate the request and discuss effort estimation in the next steering\\ncommittee meeting.\\nThe client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access\\nthe portal remotely. The request will be reviewed separately.\\nA Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\\nThe client team agreed to provide API credentials, VPN access, and production environment details\\nbefore the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"before the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\\n• Client to enable VPN connectivity for integration testing.\\n• QA team to begin CRM Integration testing.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Minutes of Meeting (MoM) / Weekly Status Report\\nProject: Internal Support Portal Implementation\\nDate: 18 April 2026\\nLocation: Microsoft Teams\\nAttendees: Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Lead, QA Lead, Client Representative\\nAgenda\\n• Review implementation progress.\\n• Discuss open blockers.\\n• Review client enhancement requests.\\n• Plan activities for next sprint.\\nDiscussion Summary\\nCRM Integration development has been completed and handed over to the QA team for system\\ntesting.\\nConfiguration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold because VPN connectivity and API\\ncredentials from the client are still pending.\\nDevelopment of the Analytics Dashboard is progressing well and is estimated to be around 60%\\ncomplete.\\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT) has been rescheduled because dependent integration activities\\nhave not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"• Project Manager to assess SAP Integration request.\\n• Technical team to prepare the UAT environment.\\nNext Meeting: 25 April 2026\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}]','2026-07-27 13:20:50'),(7,3,'USER','Does the Azure AD SSO configuration account for multi-factor authentication requirements?',NULL,'2026-07-27 13:21:32'),(8,3,'ASSISTANT','I cannot find the answer in the project documents.\n\nThe provided project documentation and baseline items specify that the vendor is responsible for configuring Azure AD SSO by 25 April 2026, as noted in the Sample Engagement Letter With Milestones (1).pdf (Page 1). However, none of the available documentation or meeting minutes contains details regarding specific security requirements, such as whether multi-factor authentication is included or accounted for in that configuration.','[{\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Azure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\\nCustomer shall provide required infrastructure before implementation.\\nChange Control\\nAny work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Sample Engagement Letter (ACSE Test Document)\\nProject Scope\\nThe Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal.\\nThe Vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search.\\nThe Vendor shall implement CRM Integration by 15 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall configure Azure AD SSO by 25 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall develop an Analytics Dashboard.\\nThe Vendor shall conduct UAT by 15 May 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall perform Production Deployment (Go Live) on 30 June 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall provide Knowledge Transfer by 05 July 2026.\\nOut of Scope\\nNative Android and iOS applications are excluded.\\nVoice Bot implementation is out of scope.\\nThird-party software licenses remain customer responsibility.\\n24x7 Production Support is not included in this engagement.\\nMilestones\\nCRM Integration - 15 April 2026\\nAzure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Minutes of Meeting (MoM) / Weekly Status Report\\nProject: Internal Support Portal Implementation\\nDate: 18 April 2026\\nLocation: Microsoft Teams\\nAttendees: Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Lead, QA Lead, Client Representative\\nAgenda\\n• Review implementation progress.\\n• Discuss open blockers.\\n• Review client enhancement requests.\\n• Plan activities for next sprint.\\nDiscussion Summary\\nCRM Integration development has been completed and handed over to the QA team for system\\ntesting.\\nConfiguration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold because VPN connectivity and API\\ncredentials from the client are still pending.\\nDevelopment of the Analytics Dashboard is progressing well and is estimated to be around 60%\\ncomplete.\\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT) has been rescheduled because dependent integration activities\\nhave not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"before the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\\n• Client to enable VPN connectivity for integration testing.\\n• QA team to begin CRM Integration testing.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"• Project Manager to assess SAP Integration request.\\n• Technical team to prepare the UAT environment.\\nNext Meeting: 25 April 2026\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"have not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\\nKnowledge Transfer sessions will be finalized after confirmation of the deployment timeline.\\nDuring the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform. The\\nproject manager agreed to evaluate the request and discuss effort estimation in the next steering\\ncommittee meeting.\\nThe client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access\\nthe portal remotely. The request will be reviewed separately.\\nA Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\\nThe client team agreed to provide API credentials, VPN access, and production environment details\\nbefore the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}]','2026-07-27 13:21:32'),(9,4,'USER','Does the CRM Integration scope include data migration from legacy systems per the EL?',NULL,'2026-07-27 13:22:02'),(10,4,'ASSISTANT','The provided project documents do not include data migration from legacy systems as part of the CRM Integration scope.\n\n1. **Scope Definition**: According to the Sample Engagement Letter With Milestones (Page 1), the CRM Integration is defined only as \"The Vendor shall implement CRM Integration by 15 April 2026.\" There is no mention of data migration requirements or legacy system integration within the structured scope items or the project engagement letter.\n\n2. **Project Status**: The Minutes of Meeting/Weekly Status Report (Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf, Page 1) confirms that CRM Integration development has been completed and handed over for testing. The current discussion regarding integration focuses on API credentials and VPN connectivity to support the existing infrastructure, rather than legacy data migration.\n\n3. **Change Control**: As stated in the Sample Engagement Letter (Page 1), any work falling beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request process. Since data migration is not currently listed as an in-scope item, it would be subject to this change control requirement.','[{\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Sample Engagement Letter (ACSE Test Document)\\nProject Scope\\nThe Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal.\\nThe Vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search.\\nThe Vendor shall implement CRM Integration by 15 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall configure Azure AD SSO by 25 April 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall develop an Analytics Dashboard.\\nThe Vendor shall conduct UAT by 15 May 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall perform Production Deployment (Go Live) on 30 June 2026.\\nThe Vendor shall provide Knowledge Transfer by 05 July 2026.\\nOut of Scope\\nNative Android and iOS applications are excluded.\\nVoice Bot implementation is out of scope.\\nThird-party software licenses remain customer responsibility.\\n24x7 Production Support is not included in this engagement.\\nMilestones\\nCRM Integration - 15 April 2026\\nAzure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"before the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\\n• Client to enable VPN connectivity for integration testing.\\n• QA team to begin CRM Integration testing.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Minutes of Meeting (MoM) / Weekly Status Report\\nProject: Internal Support Portal Implementation\\nDate: 18 April 2026\\nLocation: Microsoft Teams\\nAttendees: Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Lead, QA Lead, Client Representative\\nAgenda\\n• Review implementation progress.\\n• Discuss open blockers.\\n• Review client enhancement requests.\\n• Plan activities for next sprint.\\nDiscussion Summary\\nCRM Integration development has been completed and handed over to the QA team for system\\ntesting.\\nConfiguration of Azure AD Single Sign-On is currently on hold because VPN connectivity and API\\ncredentials from the client are still pending.\\nDevelopment of the Analytics Dashboard is progressing well and is estimated to be around 60%\\ncomplete.\\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT) has been rescheduled because dependent integration activities\\nhave not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"have not yet finished.\\nThe Go Live schedule may require revision if the current infrastructure dependencies are not\\nresolved during the coming week.\\nKnowledge Transfer sessions will be finalized after confirmation of the deployment timeline.\\nDuring the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform. The\\nproject manager agreed to evaluate the request and discuss effort estimation in the next steering\\ncommittee meeting.\\nThe client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access\\nthe portal remotely. The request will be reviewed separately.\\nA Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\\nThe client team agreed to provide API credentials, VPN access, and production environment details\\nbefore the next project review.\\nCRM Integration completion was reconfirmed during the status review.\\nAction Items\\n• Client to provide API credentials before the next review meeting.\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"• Project Manager to assess SAP Integration request.\\n• Technical team to prepare the UAT environment.\\nNext Meeting: 25 April 2026\", \"document_id\": 21, \"document_name\": \"Sample_MoM_Status_Report_Realistic.pdf\"}, {\"page\": 1, \"text\": \"Azure AD SSO - 25 April 2026\\nUAT - 15 May 2026\\nGo Live - 30 June 2026\\nKnowledge Transfer - 05 July 2026\\nAssumptions\\nCustomer shall provide VPN connectivity.\\nCustomer shall provide API credentials.\\nCustomer shall provide required infrastructure before implementation.\\nChange Control\\nAny work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\", \"document_id\": 20, \"document_name\": \"Sample_Engagement_Letter_With_Milestones (1).pdf\"}]','2026-07-27 13:22:02');
