, is not explicitly included in the approved scope baseline. While \'AI Knowledge Search\' is in scope, a customer chatbot represents a distinct conversational AI functionality beyond just knowledge search. The project team has already indicated this request would require a formal commercial review, as per the Change Control clause (\'Any work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval\'). Additionally, \'Voice Bot implementation\' is explicitly listed as out of scope, indicating that conversational AI beyond defined search functions typically requires separate approval. (Confidence: 95%)',1,'OPEN','2026-07-27 04:48:23',NULL,NULL,NULL),(21,5,8,'ACTIVITY',NULL,'The Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal',1,80,'HIGH','SCOPE_CREEP',0.9900,'Activity: Client informally asked whether a customer chatbot could be added in future\nThe approved scope includes \'The Vendor shall build a web-based Internal Support Portal\' and \'The Vendor shall implement AI Knowledge Search\'. A \'customer chatbot\' is not explicitly listed, targets an external audience (customers vs. internal staff), and implies new functionality beyond the current \'Internal Support Portal\'. This inquiry represents a potential expansion of scope that is not currently approved. (Confidence: 95%)\n\n[Update]: Activity: Team clarified this would require commercial review (for customer chatbot)\nThis activity directly indicates that the requested \'customer chatbot\' functionality is considered \'beyond the approved scope\' by the vendor\'s team. As per the Change Control clause in SOURCE 2B, \'Any work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\' This clarifies a need for a formal commercial review for this new, unapproved request. (Confidence: 98%)\n\n[Update]: Activity: No decision taken (regarding customer chatbot)\nThis activity tracks the status of the \'customer chatbot\' request, which has already been identified as requiring a commercial review. Since no decision has been taken, the item remains unapproved and continues to require formal review as it falls outside the current contractual scope. (Confidence: 90%)\n\n[Update]: Activity: Customer Chatbot Implementation Request\nThe activity is not explicitly in the approved scope baseline [1-8]. SOURCE 2A (ChromaDB) explicitly states \'Voice Bot implementation is out of scope\'. Additionally, SOURCE 2B (ChromaDB) \'Change Control\' states \'Any work beyond the approved scope requires a formal Change Request approval.\' The client\'s informal request for a \'customer chatbot\' falls outside the defined deliverables and is explicitly excluded, requiring formal review. (Confidence: 99%)',1,'OPEN','2026-07-27 04:48:42',NULL,NULL,NULL),(22,7,11,'ACTIVITY',NULL,'SAP Integration',1,80,'HIGH','SCOPE_CREEP',0.9000,'Activity: SAP Integration\nMoM Evidence: During the meeting, the client requested SAP Integration with the existing ERP platform.\nAnalysis: SAP Integration is not included in the baseline Project Scope, which only authorizes CRM Integration. This is a new client scope request. (Confidence: 90%)',1,'OPEN','2026-07-27 05:06:07',NULL,NULL,NULL),(23,7,11,'ACTIVITY',NULL,'Mobile Applications',1,80,'HIGH','SCOPE_CREEP',0.9000,'Activity: Mobile Applications\nMoM Evidence: The client also requested Android and iOS mobile applications to enable field engineers to access the portal remotely.\nAnalysis: The approved Project Scope only covers a web-based Internal Support Portal. Requesting separate Android and iOS mobile applications constitutes major scope creep. (Confidence: 90%)',1,'OPEN','2026-07-27 05:06:20',NULL,NULL,NULL),(24,7,11,'ACTIVITY',NULL,'Voice Bot implementation is out of scope',1,50,'MEDIUM','SCOPE_CREEP',0.9000,'Activity: Voice Bot implementation is out of scope\nMoM Evidence: A Voice Bot capability for customer support was proposed for future consideration.\nAnalysis: A Voice Bot capability is not part of the approved Project Scope. Althou